    'FluxVectorController/SpeedFluxObserver/FluxObserver', 'FluxObserver (motulator)', 'Flux observer in estimated rotor coordinates (FluxObserver). The observer uses the voltage u_s_zoh_ab of the ongoing sampling period, and the output fbk.u_s is the voltage u_s_ab averaged over the previous and ongoing periods (DriveControlSystem.get_feedback). In standby, the voltages are unknown (NaN), and the flux estimate follows the current model alone, with the open-circuit voltage of the model as the voltage. When the voltage is known again after the release of the gates, the estimates are initialized from the current response to the zero-voltage period (the flying start of SpeedFluxObserver), and the output init = [flag w_M] initializes the SpeedObserver. In the sensored mode (h = 1), the position error signal is computed from the measured rotor angle (compute_feedback). The machine model par is a struct with the fields n_p, R_s, L_d, L_q, and psi_f of SynchronousMachinePars, or n_p, R_s, and psi_s_dq_fcn (a GradNet flux map) of SaturatedSynchronousMachinePars.', strjoin({ ...
